</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion, Limitations, and Future Works</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper theoretically studies the learning dynamics, ICL generalization, and the robustness to outliers of Mamba models, together with a characterization of how different components of Mamba contribute to the ICL mechanism. Our analysis also provides a theoretical comparison between Mamba and linear Transformer models. Although based on a one-layer Mamba structure on binary classification tasks, this work provides a deeper theoretical understanding and provable advantages of Mamba. Future directions include designing general Mamba-based language/multi-modal models.</p>
</div>
</section>
