<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E160Xj.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{\eta(1-p_{a})\beta^{2}(t_{0}+1)}{M_{1}}-\sum_{i=1}^{t_{0}}i^{2}\cdot(\frac{\eta^{3}(1-p_{a})^{3}\beta^{2}}{M_{1}^{3}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{\eta(1-p_{a})\beta^{2}(t_{0}+1)}{M_{1}}-\sum_{i=1}^{t_{0}}i^{2}\cdot(\frac{\eta^{3}(1-p_{a})^{3}\beta^{2}}{M_{1}^{3}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.21" class="ltx_p">where the second step of (<a href="#A5.E160" title="In Proof. ‣ E.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix E Proof of Supportive Lemmas ‣ Can Mamba Learn In Context with Outliers? A Theoretical Generalization Analysis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">160</span></a>) follows the second step in (<a href="#A5.E142" title="In Proof. ‣ E.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix E Proof of Supportive Lemmas ‣ Can Mamba Learn In Context with Outliers? A Theoretical Generalization Analysis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">142</span></a>) using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ Appendix C Key Lemmas ‣ Can Mamba Learn In Context with Outliers? A Theoretical Generalization Analysis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Meanwhile,</p>
